---
import EchoesRecordFlow from '../../components/EchoesRecordFlow.astro';
import EchoesDiagram from '../../components/EchoesDiagram.astro';
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import ProjectHeader from '../../components/ProjectHeader.astro';
import ProjectFooter from '../../components/ProjectFooter.astro';
const description = 'A time-rewind puzzle game for GMTK Game Jam 2025. Programming, game design, and five progressive levels plus a hidden ending.';
const lessons = [
  { n: 1, title: 'Meet your past self', text: 'Introduce the hourglass and rewind. The player creates an echo that repeats their previous actions, then continues from their current position.' },
  { n: 2, title: 'Recover time, keep your ground', text: 'A deliberately short countdown makes a direct run fail. Rewinding restores the countdown while preserving the distance the player has already covered.' },
  { n: 3, title: 'Leave someone at the switch', text: 'For the first time, an echo must hold a pressure plate. The player records time on the plate, rewinds, and uses that window to pass through the gate.' },
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><BaseHead title="Echoes of Time — Chao Bian" description={description} /></head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<ProjectHeader />
<main id="main">
<section class="hero wrap">
  <div class="kicker"><span>GAME DESIGN & DEVELOPMENT / 2025</span><span>GMTK GAME JAM · THEME: LOOP</span></div>
  <h1>Echoes<br />of <em>Time.</em></h1>
  <div class="intro"><p>A 2D puzzle game where rewinding time turns your past actions into a physical partner, creating puzzles of timing, passage, and cooperation.</p><a class="button" href="https://jietiao.itch.io/echoes-of-time" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Play on itch.io ↗</a></div>
  <figure><img class="cover" src="/projects/echoes-of-time/cover.webp" alt="Echoes of Time title screen in a pixel-art stone courtyard" width="1600" height="877" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption>GMTK GAME JAM 2025 / ECHOES OF TIME</figcaption></figure>
  <dl class="metadata"><div><dt>DEVELOPMENT</dt><dd>Solo · 2 days</dd></div><div><dt>MY ROLE</dt><dd>Programming · Game Design · Level Design</dd></div><div><dt>ENGINE</dt><dd>Unity · C#</dd></div><div><dt>CONTENT</dt><dd>5 levels + 1 hidden ending level</dd></div></dl>
  <p class="credits">Built with external art and audio assets. <a href="https://jietiao.itch.io/echoes-of-time#:~:text=Credits" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Asset credits on itch.io ↗</a></p>
</section>
<nav class="chapters" aria-label="Project sections"><div class="wrap"><a href="#mechanic">01 / The mechanic</a><a href="#progression">02 / Learning the rules</a><a href="#design">03 / Two design processes</a><a href="#ending">04 / Breaking the loop</a></div></nav>
<section id="mechanic" class="section wrap">
  <div class="split"><header><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE CORE IDEA</p><h2>Your past becomes<br />part of the puzzle.</h2></header><div><p>The jam theme “Loop” led me to time loops, then to rewind. I designed and programmed a system where rewinding creates an echo of the player’s recorded actions. The player stays at their current position while the echo returns to the beginning of its recording.</p><p>Once time moves forward again, the two share the same physical space. An echo can hold a switch, open a route, or block the player in a narrow passage.</p></div></div>
  <ol class="rules"><li><span>01 / RECORD</span><h3>Make a plan.</h3><p>Move, wait, or keep moving toward a closed gate. Plan the actions you want your echo to repeat.</p></li><li><span>02 / REWIND</span><h3>Stay. Turn time back.</h3><p>Press R to rewind the recording and recover countdown time. The player cannot stop rewind early.</p></li><li><span>03 / REPLAY</span><h3>Act alongside the echo.</h3><p>The echo repeats the recorded movement, then fades out. Its limited duration makes waiting part of the plan.</p></li></ol>

</section>
<section id="progression" class="tinted"><div class="section wrap">
  <header class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / A PROGRESSIVE INTRODUCTION</p><h2>Teach one consequence<br />at a time.</h2><p>The first three levels separate the system’s ideas: creating an echo, recovering time without losing position, and using a past action to change the environment.</p></header>
  <div class="lessons">{lessons.map(level => <article><figure>{level.n === 2 ? <video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/projects/echoes-of-time/time-restored.webp" aria-label="Level two: restoring the countdown without changing the player's position"><source src="/projects/echoes-of-time/time-restored.mp4" type="video/mp4" /></video> : level.n === 3 ? <EchoesDiagram stage="lesson" /> : <img src={`/projects/echoes-of-time/level${level.n}.webp`} alt={level.n === 1 ? 'Player and echo together after rewind in the starting courtyard' : 'Echo holds the pressure plate while Player passes through the open gate'} width="1280" height="718" loading="lazy" />}<figcaption>{level.n === 2 ? 'Gameplay excerpt · Normal speed · Captioned' : 'GAMEPLAY STILL'}</figcaption></figure><span class="eyebrow">LEVEL 0{level.n}</span><h3>{level.title}</h3><p>{level.text}</p></article>)}</div>
</div></section>
<section id="design" class="section wrap">
  <header class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / FROM SYSTEM TO LEVEL</p><h2>Two puzzles.<br />Two ways of finding them.</h2><p>Level four grew from an unexpected behavior in testing. Level five began with a planned solution that shaped the implementation.</p></header>
  <article class="case"><div class="split"><div><p class="eyebrow">LEVEL 04 / A DISCOVERY IN TESTING</p><h3>Make room for your past self.</h3><p>Testing revealed that the player and echoes could physically block each other. After considering whether to remove that behavior, I kept it and designed a level around a shared narrow passage.</p><p>The player must coordinate route and timing with the echo: which one enters first, when to wait, and how to leave room for the other to pass. Recording a successful route is only half of the solution; the player must also be able to coexist with it.</p></div><aside class="insight"><dl><div><dt>Origin</dt><dd>Discovered during testing</dd></div><div><dt>Constraint</dt><dd>Shared narrow passage</dd></div></dl></aside></div>
  <figure class="annotated"><EchoesDiagram stage="passage" /><figcaption>Player and Echo must use the same narrow passage between the two left-hand walls. Solid-body collision makes their timing part of the puzzle.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/projects/echoes-of-time/passage-poster.webp" aria-label="Level four walkthrough showing the shared narrow passage"><source src="/projects/echoes-of-time/passage-timing.mp4" type="video/mp4" /></video><figcaption>LEVEL 04 / 21-SECOND TIMING EXCERPT · NORMAL SPEED · GAME AUDIO</figcaption></figure></article>
  <article class="case"><div class="split"><div><p class="eyebrow">LEVEL 05 / A PLANNED INTERDEPENDENCE</p><h3>Help the echo help you.</h3><p>I designed this level around mutual dependence: the player creates the conditions for the echo to advance, and the echo returns the favor. Each actor must enable the other’s next action.</p></div><aside class="insight"><dl><div><dt>Origin</dt><dd>Planned puzzle solution</dd></div><div><dt>Requirement</dt><dd>Replay responds to changed gate states</dd></div></dl></aside></div>
  <p class="diagram-legend"><span class="legend-move">→</span> Movement <span class="legend-link">┄</span> Active switch → matching gate · A and B identify the same mechanisms in every view. The camera follows Player.</p>
  <div class="sequence" aria-label="Level five solution in three stages">
    <figure><EchoesDiagram stage="record" /><figcaption><strong>01 / Record</strong>Keep moving against closed Gate A even while it blocks the player. Echo will replay this sustained movement when the gate opens.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><EchoesDiagram stage="enable" /><figcaption><strong>02 / Enable</strong>After rewind, Player holds Switch A. Echo passes through Gate A toward Switch B.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><EchoesDiagram stage="cooperate" /><figcaption><strong>03 / Cooperate</strong>Echo activates Switch B, opening Gate B for Player to pass through.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/projects/echoes-of-time/cooperation-poster.webp" aria-label="Level five walkthrough showing the player and echo opening gates for each other"><source src="/projects/echoes-of-time/cooperative-solution.mp4" type="video/mp4" /></video><figcaption>LEVEL 05 / CONTINUOUS SOLUTION · Rewind sped up 2× in editing; all other actions at normal speed · GAME AUDIO</figcaption></figure></article>
  <div class="implementation"><header><p class="eyebrow">IMPLEMENTATION / SUPPORTING THE INTENDED SOLUTION</p><h3>Restore positions backward.<br />Apply velocity forward.</h3></header>
  <EchoesRecordFlow />
  <div class="implementation-notes"><p><code>Record.cs</code> stores Position, Velocity, and Sprite in a linked list during <code>LateUpdate</code>. <code>PlayerAgent.cs</code> reads it in either direction; <code>GameManager</code> restores countdown time during rewind.</p><p><strong>Recording:</strong> Gate A is closed. The player is blocked but keeps trying to move.<br /><strong>Replay:</strong> Player opens Gate A. The recorded velocity carries Echo through.</p></div></div>
</section>
<section id="ending" class="tinted"><div class="section wrap">
  <header class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">04 / HIDDEN LEVEL 0</p><h2>One last loop.<br /><em>A different intention.</em></h2><p>Unlocked after level five, the hidden ending returns to the starting courtyard. The player’s goal changes from helping their past self to stopping them.</p></header>
  <div class="ending-design"><figure><img src="/projects/echoes-of-time/level0.webp" alt="Player and Echo meet again in the starting courtyard in hidden level zero" width="1280" height="718" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>HIDDEN LEVEL 0 / RETURN TO THE STARTING COURTYARD</figcaption></figure><div><blockquote>“Go back. Stop yourself—stop me—before we ever touch the hourglass.”</blockquote><p>Earlier levels ask the player to cooperate with their past self. The ending reverses that relationship: take the hourglass first and stop the loop from beginning.</p></div></div>
  <details class="spoiler"><summary>Watch the story & ending excerpt</summary><div class="spoiler-content"><figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/projects/echoes-of-time/ending-excerpt.webp" aria-label="Hidden level zero and its ending dialogue"><source src="/projects/echoes-of-time/ending-excerpt.mp4" type="video/mp4" /></video><figcaption>HIDDEN LEVEL 0 / ENDING EXCERPT · NORMAL SPEED · GAME AUDIO</figcaption></figure></div></details>
</div></section>
<section class="section wrap reflection"><p class="eyebrow">PLAYER FEEDBACK & NEXT STEPS</p><h2>Keep the cooperation.<br />Revisit the pacing.</h2><p>Players responded positively to the progression between levels and the ending’s reversal. Several comments also highlighted long rewind waits and slow movement; one player reported finishing level four with only 0.15 seconds remaining.</p><p>My next step is to test faster rewind playback and recalibrate level time limits around the revised pacing. I would also test movement speed separately to understand how it affects passage timing. These changes are planned and have not been implemented.</p><a href="https://itch.io/jam/gmtk-2025/rate/3784181" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the player feedback ↗</a></section>

</main>
<ProjectFooter />
</body>
</html>
